[1m[38;5;231mHow should the system decide a user "cares about" a task?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mBoth: auto-subscribe + watch (Recommended)[39m
     [38;5;246mImplicit rules (assigned, created, commented) auto-subscribe you; an explicit watch/mute button overrides. One [39m
     [38;5;246msubscriptions table, no migration later.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m Implicit only
     [38;5;246mAssignee/creator/commenter get notified. No UI, fastest to build. Can't express 'stop telling me about this' [39m
     [38;5;246mwithout a later migration.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m Explicit watching only
     [38;5;246mUsers click watch. Precise and quiet, but relies on people remembering to opt in — usually under-adopted.[39m
  [38;5;246m4.[39m Project/team-level
     [38;5;246mYou subscribe to a project or list, not individual tasks. Simpler mental model, much noisier per notification.[39m
  [38;5;246m5. Type something.[39m
